cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LibKa in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LibKa Design Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Libor Klimeš (aivigator.ai)"
version: "2.0.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aivigator-ai/open-libka-design-platform"
url: "https://libka.aivigator.ai/"
abstract: >-
  LibKa is a design system (W3C DTCG design tokens) and a document platform. One Markdown file with LibKa blocks
  becomes a web page, an A4 PDF, 16:9 slides and an editable Word file, each checked for accessibility (axe-core
  WCAG 2.2 A/AA, text contrast, structure rules, reflow at 320 CSS pixels, veraPDF PDF/UA-1, the Word file's structure), with a signed manifest
  of the checks.
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - wcag
  - pdf-ua
  - markdown
  - design-tokens
  - docs-as-code
  - slides
  - mcp
